    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer planar dielectric stack on a SiO2 (Gao) substrate (representing fused silica) with Air incidence. Materials must alternate between Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Gao), starting with Ta2O5 (Gao) at the air interface. Define 36 independent thickness variables, one per layer, bounded between 20 nm and 350 nm. Simulate transmittance from 350 nm to 1100 nm with sufficient resolution to cover 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, and 1030-1080 nm bands. Objective: Maximize average transmittance in 420-700 nm, minimize average transmittance in 355-365 nm, and minimize average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. Initialize optimization with layer thicknesses approximating quarter-wave optical thickness at 600 nm (Ta2O5 (Gao) ~100 nm, SiO2 (Gao) ~220 nm) to break symmetry. Incidence angle 0 deg, unpolarized light.",
